            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for gardening, then the Spanish for to sew."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: el calentamiento",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el calentamiento — \"the warm-up; warming\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Antes de correr hago diez minutos de calentamiento. Before running I do a ten-minute warm-up."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "El calentamiento global — global warming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "calentamiento is built on calentar \"to warm\", made from caliente \"hot\" (EtymDB), which comes from Latin calēns, from calēre \"to be warm\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
